{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AtomicityJetIndependence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.AtomicityJetIndependence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.PlanckStepAtomicity","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WellFounded"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.jet_order_strengthenings_still_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.jet_order_strengthenings_still_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L360-L379","doc":"**The strengthened axiom set is STILL insufficient (proved,\nsorry-free, unconditional).** One and the same rank-2 model satisfies\nthe full jet-compatibility axiom set PLUS totality PLUS the existence\nof a least nonzero step PLUS cofinality of that step's iterates — and\nis still not atomic. So no order-theoretic strengthening of\n`prop:ordering-jet-compatibility` along these natural axes can close\nroute 1: what atomicity adds is precisely the `generates` clause (every\nsegment IS an iterate of the step, not merely comparable to iterates),\nand any jet-tower formalization strong enough to imply it would have to\ncarry that clause as an assumption — i.e. assume the conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.e1_iterates_cofinal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.e1_iterates_cofinal","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L351-L358","doc":"The minimal step's iterates are COFINAL: every element is strictly\nbelow some `n • (1,0)`. Even \"the Planck step's iterates exhaust the\norder cofinally\" does not force atomicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.e1_least_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.e1_least_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L331-L349","doc":"The model even has a genuine \"Planck step\": `(1,0)` is the LEAST\nnonzero element of the total order `degLexPair`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.nsmul_e1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.nsmul_e1","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L325-L329","doc":"Iterates of the first generator: `n • (1,0) = (n,0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair_trichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair_trichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L308-L323","doc":"The rank-2 model order is TOTAL: trichotomy holds. So upgrading the\njet-compatibility axioms from \"admissible ordering\" to \"total\ntranslation-invariant well-order\" still cannot force atomicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.planckStepAtomicity_independent_of_jet_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.planckStepAtomicity_independent_of_jet_order","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L287-L304","doc":"**Full independence (proved, sorry-free, unconditional).** The\njet-compatibility axiom set neither proves nor refutes atomicity:\n`ℕ × ℕ` carries a jet-compatible order and is not atomic\n(`planckStepAtomicity_not_forced_by_jet_order`), while `ℕ` carries a\njet-compatible order and is atomic (`rankOneJetOrder`,\n`nat_is_atomic`). Atomicity is genuinely NEW content beyond the\njet-tower ordering structure — which is exactly the situation the\n§3b-tax primary-conjecture-class representation of\n`PlanckStepAtomicity` is designed for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.planckStepAtomicity_not_forced_by_jet_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.planckStepAtomicity_not_forced_by_jet_order","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L270-L285","doc":"**Route 1 closes negative (proved, sorry-free, unconditional).**\nThe jet-compatibility axiom set does NOT force atomicity: it is\nrefutable to claim that every additive monoid carrying a\njet-compatible order is atomic. Witness: `rankTwoJetOrder` on `ℕ × ℕ`\nsatisfies every leg, yet `ℕ × ℕ` has no single generating step\n(`atomicity_fails_for_two_generators`). Consequently there is no\ntheorem `JetCompatibleOrder M → PlanckStepAtomicity M`, and\n`prop:ordering-jet-compatibility`'s order structure cannot upgrade\n`PlanckStepAtomicity` from premise to theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.nat_is_atomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.nat_is_atomic","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L259-L266","doc":"`ℕ` IS atomic: the step `1` generates freely. Stated as a raw\nexistential — deliberately NOT a `PlanckStepAtomicity` instance, to\nkeep the class's instance count at zero (its no-instance discipline is\nthe honest open-state marker for the substrate's monoid). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.rankOneJetOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.rankOneJetOrder","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L246-L257","doc":"**The rank-1 model.** `ℕ` with its usual order also satisfies every\nleg (trivial one-generator filtration) — so the axiom set is consistent\nwith atomicity as well as with its failure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.rankTwoJetOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.rankTwoJetOrder","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L221-L242","doc":"**The rank-2 model.** `ℕ × ℕ` satisfies EVERY leg of the\njet-compatibility axiom set: `degLexPair` order, alphabet filtration in\nwhich the second generator `(0,1)` is the level-1 jet-prolongation\ndirection (level 0 = the submonoid on the first generator; level ≥ 1 =\neverything). All fields proved, sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair_compat","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L212-L219","doc":"`degLexPair` is translation-invariant — leg 2\n(`ordering_compatible`) for the rank-2 model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair_wf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair_wf","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L197-L210","doc":"`degLexPair` is well-founded — the same length-first factoring\nthrough `Prod.Lex` as the block's `degLex_wf_unrestricted`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.degLexPair","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L187-L195","doc":"Degree-lexicographic order on the rank-two step monoid `ℕ × ℕ` —\nthe exact analogue of the block's `degLex` (length first, then lex):\ncompare total degree first, then the second (\"jet-direction\")\ncoordinate. At fixed degree the pair is determined by its second\ncoordinate, so this IS the full lex tie-break. Note the new generator\n`(0,1)` is ordered AFTER the old one `(1,0)`, exactly as the jet\nprolongation orders new Ω¹ directions after all old generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.terminates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.terminates","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L177-L181","doc":"**Direct-limit termination leg (leg 4), derived.** The block's\n`axiom direct_limit_terminates` concludes `∃ w', ¬ degLex w' w`; that\nshape follows from irreflexivity alone (take `w' = w`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.lt_irrefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.lt_irrefl","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L171-L175","doc":"A well-founded relation is irreflexive (self-contained; used for the\ntermination leg). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.ltAt_wellFounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.ltAt_wellFounded","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L165-L169","doc":"**Per-level well-foundedness**, mirroring the block's\n`wellfounded_at_level`: each restriction of a well-founded relation is\nwell-founded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.ltAt_extends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.ltAt_extends","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L157-L163","doc":"**Extension leg (leg 1), derived.** The level-`(n)` ordering extends\nto every later level — the non-tautological content of the block's\n`axiom ordering_extends`, recovered here from `level_mono` because the\nordering is one global relation restricted to levels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.ltAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.ltAt","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L152-L155","doc":"The level-`n` restriction of the ordering — the block Lean's\n`degLex w w' ∧ ∀ g ∈ w, g < n` shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.wf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.wf","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L146-L146","doc":"Leg 3 (`wellfounded_at_level`, globally): no infinite descent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.compat","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L144-L144","doc":"Leg 2 (`ordering_compatible`): two-sided translation invariance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.level_exhausts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.level_exhausts","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L142-L142","doc":"Direct-limit leg: every element lives at some finite level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.level_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.level_mono","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L140-L140","doc":"The tower is increasing: the prolongation `ℓ_n` embeds level `m`\ninto every later level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.add_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.add_mem","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L137-L137","doc":"Each level is closed under composition (subalgebra closure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.zero_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.zero_mem","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Each level contains the empty computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.level","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L133-L133","doc":"The jet filtration: membership in the level-`n` subalgebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.lt","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L131-L131","doc":"The braiding-induced ordering (global; levels restrict it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder.mk","kind":"ctor","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.SubstrateClock.JetCompatibleOrder","kind":"structure","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/AtomicityJetIndependence.lean#L111-L146","doc":"Abstract extraction of the `prop:ordering-jet-compatibility` axiom\nset for an additive computation monoid `M` — the strongest structural\nreading under which the jet-tower ordering could bear on\n`PlanckStepAtomicity` at all:\n\n* `lt` — the braiding-induced ordering (one GLOBAL relation, exactly as\n  the block Lean's `degLex`; per-level orderings are its restrictions,\n  which is why the block's `axiom ordering_extends` is tautological\n  there and the extension leg is the derived `ltAt_extends` here);\n* `level` — the jet filtration `A₀ ⊆ A₁ ⊆ …`: an increasing exhaustive\n  tower of submonoids (`zero_mem`/`add_mem` = subalgebra closure,\n  `level_mono` = the prolongation embeddings `ℓ_n`, `level_exhausts` =\n  the direct-limit leg);\n* `compat` — leg 2, translation invariance (`ordering_compatible`);\n* `wf` — leg 3, well-foundedness (`wellfounded_at_level`, globally).\n\nThis is a `structure`, not a class: an ordering is a CHOICE of data, and\na monoid may carry several. ","signatureChunk":0}]}